{
    "background_story": "Maximus was a majestic goldfish who lived in a cozy aquarium. He loved to swim lazily around his castle-shaped decoration, chasing the occasional flake of food. However, Maximus had a weakness for overeating. His owner, a kind old man, would often feed him too much, thinking it would make him happy. But the excess food would cause Maximus's belly to bloat, making it hard for him to swim. One day, his owner realized the error of his ways and started feeding Maximus a balanced diet. With time, Maximus's bloated belly returned to its normal size, and he could once again dart around his tank with ease. Despite his struggles with bloat, Maximus remained a gentle giant, always greeting his owner with a friendly fin wave.",
